## Implementation Overview

Refactor `RoutineEditorPage.tsx` from add-only mode to full editing mode. The page already handles routine name editing (lines 54-62, 161-181), exercise deletion (lines 118-124), and drag-and-drop reordering (lines 126-137, 183-258) via `@hello-pangea/dnd`. Extend this pattern to enable inline editing of individual exercise fields.

## Key Architecture Patterns to Follow

**Existing patterns from codebase:**
- **State management**: Currently uses `useState` + direct Supabase calls (no React Query mutations yet in RoutineEditorPage, unlike WorkoutSessionPage which uses React Query heavily per Task 5)
- **Offline-first**: React Query configured with `networkMode: 'offlineFirst'` in `src/lib/queryClient.ts:28-32`
- **Drag-and-drop**: Already implemented with `@hello-pangea/dnd` for exercise reordering (lines 183-258)
- **Inline editing pattern**: Routine name already uses inline edit mode with input field + Save/Cancel buttons (lines 161-181)
- **Data persistence**: Direct Supabase updates via `supabase.from('exercises').update()` pattern

## Implementation Steps

### 1. Add Exercise Editing State

Extend state management in `RoutineEditorPage.tsx`:

```tsx
const [editingExercise, setEditingExercise] = useState<string | null>(null)
const [exerciseEdits, setExerciseEdits] = useState<{
  [id: string]: {
    name?: string
    machine_info?: string
    target_sets_reps?: string
    starting_weight_kg?: number
  }
}>({})
```

### 2. Create Inline Exercise Editor Component

Create `src/components/ExerciseItemEditor.tsx` to replace the read-only exercise display (current lines 190-250):

```tsx
interface ExerciseItemEditorProps {
  exercise: Exercise
  isEditing: boolean
  isDragging: boolean
  dragHandleProps: any
  onEdit: () => void
  onSave: (updates: ExerciseUpdates) => Promise<void>
  onCancel: () => void
  onDelete: () => void
  onDeleteMedia?: () => void
}

export default function ExerciseItemEditor({
  exercise,
  isEditing,
  isDragging,
  dragHandleProps,
  onEdit,
  onSave,
  onCancel,
  onDelete,
  onDeleteMedia
}: ExerciseItemEditorProps) {
  const [localName, setLocalName] = useState(exercise.name)
  const [localMachineInfo, setLocalMachineInfo] = useState(exercise.machine_info ?? '')
  const [localTargetSetsReps, setLocalTargetSetsReps] = useState(exercise.target_sets_reps ?? '')

  // Reset local state when switching to edit mode
  useEffect(() => {
    if (isEditing) {
      setLocalName(exercise.name)
      setLocalMachineInfo(exercise.machine_info ?? '')
      setLocalTargetSetsReps(exercise.target_sets_reps ?? '')
    }
  }, [isEditing, exercise])

  const handleSave = async () => {
    await onSave({
      name: localName.trim() || exercise.name,
      machine_info: localMachineInfo.trim() || null,
      target_sets_reps: localTargetSetsReps.trim() || null,
    })
  }

  if (isEditing) {
    return (
      <div className={`rounded-lg border p-3 bg-blue-50 dark:bg-blue-900/20 border-blue-300 dark:border-blue-700`}>
        <div className="space-y-2">
          <input
            type="text"
            value={localName}
            onChange={(e) => setLocalName(e.target.value)}
            placeholder="Exercise name"
            className="w-full rounded border px-2 py-1 text-sm dark:bg-gray-700 dark:border-gray-600"
            autoFocus
          />
          <input
            type="text"
            value={localMachineInfo}
            onChange={(e) => setLocalMachineInfo(e.target.value)}
            placeholder="Equipment/Machine info"
            className="w-full rounded border px-2 py-1 text-sm dark:bg-gray-700 dark:border-gray-600"
          />
          <input
            type="text"
            value={localTargetSetsReps}
            onChange={(e) => setLocalTargetSetsReps(e.target.value)}
            placeholder="Target sets/reps (e.g., 3x12)"
            className="w-full rounded border px-2 py-1 text-sm dark:bg-gray-700 dark:border-gray-600"
          />
          <div className="flex gap-2 pt-1">
            <button onClick={handleSave} className="flex-1 rounded bg-green-600 px-3 py-1.5 text-sm text-white hover:bg-green-700">
              Save
            </button>
            <button onClick={onCancel} className="flex-1 rounded bg-gray-400 px-3 py-1.5 text-sm text-white hover:bg-gray-500">
              Cancel
            </button>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    )
  }

  // Read-only view (current implementation from RoutineEditorPage lines 193-250)
  return (
    <div className={`flex items-center gap-3 rounded-lg border bg-white p-3 dark:bg-gray-800 ${
      isDragging ? 'border-blue-400 shadow-lg' : 'border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700'
    }`}>
      <div {...dragHandleProps} className="cursor-grab text-gray-400 hover:text-gray-600">
        {/* Drag handle icon */}
      </div>
      {exercise.media_url && (
        <div className="group relative">
          <img src={exercise.media_url} alt={exercise.name} className="h-10 w-10 rounded object-cover" />
          {onDeleteMedia && (
            <button onClick={onDeleteMedia} className="absolute -right-1 -top-1 hidden group-hover:block rounded-full bg-red-500 p-0.5 text-white">
              {/* Delete icon */}
            </button>
          )}
        </div>
      )}
      <div className="min-w-0 flex-1" onClick={onEdit}>
        <div className="flex items-center gap-2">
          <span className="font-medium">{exercise.name}</span>
          <span className="rounded-full bg-gray-100 px-2 py-0.5 text-xs text-gray-600 dark:bg-gray-700 dark:text-gray-400">
            {exercise.muscle_group.replace('_', ' ')}
          </span>
        </div>
        <div className="mt-0.5 flex gap-3 text-xs text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400">
          {exercise.target_sets_reps && <span>{exercise.target_sets_reps}</span>}
          {exercise.machine_info && <span>{exercise.machine_info}</span>}
        </div>
      </div>
      <button onClick={onDelete} className="rounded-lg p-2 text-gray-400 hover:bg-red-50 hover:text-red-500">
        {/* Delete icon */}
      </button>
    </div>
  )
}
```

### 3. Update RoutineEditorPage to Use Editor Component

Replace the exercise list rendering (lines 190-252) with:

```tsx
{exercises.map((ex, index) => (
  <Draggable key={ex.id} draggableId={ex.id} index={index}>
    {(prov, snapshot) => (
      <div ref={prov.innerRef} {...prov.draggableProps}>
        <ExerciseItemEditor
          exercise={ex}
          isEditing={editingExercise === ex.id}
          isDragging={snapshot.isDragging}
          dragHandleProps={prov.dragHandleProps}
          onEdit={() => setEditingExercise(ex.id)}
          onSave={async (updates) => {
            await supabase
              .from('exercises')
              .update(updates)
              .eq('id', ex.id)
            setEditingExercise(null)
            await fetchRoutine()
          }}
          onCancel={() => setEditingExercise(null)}
          onDelete={() => deleteExercise(ex)}
          onDeleteMedia={ex.media_url ? () => deleteMedia(ex) : undefined}
        />
      </div>
    )}
  </Draggable>
))}
```

### 4. Add Starting Weight Field to Exercise Schema

Currently, the `exercises` table doesn't have a `starting_weight_kg` field (per `src/types/database.ts:40-74`). Add this field via Supabase migration:

```sql
ALTER TABLE exercises 
ADD COLUMN starting_weight_kg NUMERIC(5,2) DEFAULT NULL;
```

Update TypeScript types in `src/types/database.ts`:

```typescript
export interface Exercise {
  // ... existing fields
  starting_weight_kg: number | null
}
```

### 5. Integrate Starting Weight into Editor

Add to `ExerciseItemEditor`:

```tsx
const [localStartingWeight, setLocalStartingWeight] = useState(
  exercise.starting_weight_kg?.toString() ?? ''
)

// In edit mode UI:
<input
  type="number"
  step="0.5"
  value={localStartingWeight}
  onChange={(e) => setLocalStartingWeight(e.target.value)}
  placeholder="Starting weight (kg)"
  className="w-full rounded border px-2 py-1 text-sm dark:bg-gray-700 dark:border-gray-600"
/>

// In handleSave:
starting_weight_kg: localStartingWeight ? parseFloat(localStartingWeight) : null
```

### 6. Mobile UX Enhancements

- **Tap-to-edit**: Entire exercise card becomes tappable to enter edit mode (already implemented via `onClick={onEdit}` in read-only view)
- **Haptic feedback**: Use existing `src/lib/haptics.ts` for edit mode entry/exit:

```tsx
import { triggerHaptic } from '../lib/haptics'

const handleEdit = () => {
  triggerHaptic('light')
  setEditingExercise(ex.id)
}
```

- **Visual feedback**: Blue border/background in edit mode to distinguish from read-only state
- **Large touch targets**: Buttons sized for 44px minimum (current buttons are `py-1.5` ≈ 32px, increase to `py-2.5`)

### 7. Offline Sync Integration

The existing offline setup (Task 11) uses React Query Persister with IndexedDB (`src/lib/queryClient.ts`). Current implementation in RoutineEditorPage uses direct Supabase calls without React Query mutations.

**Options:**

**Option A (Minimal change)**: Keep direct Supabase calls, rely on React Query's offline-first mode for queries only. Mutations will fail offline but queue via service worker.

**Option B (Recommended)**: Migrate to React Query mutations pattern from `WorkoutSessionPage` (Task 5):

```tsx
import { useMutation, useQueryClient } from '@tanstack/react-query'

const queryClient = useQueryClient()

const updateExerciseMutation = useMutation({
  mutationFn: async ({ id, updates }: { id: string; updates: ExerciseUpdates }) => {
    const { error } = await supabase.from('exercises').update(updates).eq('id', id)
    if (error) throw error
  },
  onSuccess: () => {
    queryClient.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: ['routine', id] })
  },
})

// In save handler:
await updateExerciseMutation.mutateAsync({ id: ex.id, updates })
```

This ensures mutations queue properly when offline and sync when back online (per Task 11's offline cache layer).

### 8. Data Consistency

- **Optimistic updates**: Update local state immediately, revert on error
- **Conflict resolution**: Last-write-wins (Supabase default behavior via `updated_at` timestamp)
- **Validation**: Ensure exercise name is required (non-empty), other fields optional

